{
  "id": "kangaroo-care",
  "term": "kangaroo care",
  "definition": "Kangaroo care is a family-centered way of caring for an infant, especially in neonatal intensive care, by placing the baby in direct skin-to-skin contact on a parent's bare chest. It is used to support the infant’s physical stability and breastfeeding while also helping meet emotional needs and strengthen parental wellbeing, bonding, and attachment.",
